{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The settings deny-list's name half (unified-settings design 13, plan call 9): no agent may change these, under",
    "any grant. norn::options::deny (Rust) holds the same lists and its test `deny_table` checks them against this",
    "file; the editor's test (settings-agents-test) runs its cases and characters against the editor's check, which",
    "adds what only Lisp knows (`:agents never`, `:workspace code`).",
    "A name is denied when it is one of `names`, starts with one of `prefixes`, ends with one of `suffixes`, ends",
    "with one of `numbered_suffixes` followed by one or more digits, or holds whitespace, a control character or one of",
    "`characters` (no variable's name: the editor refuses them). Suffixes are compared case-insensitively",
    "(Emacs's risky-local-variable-p matches with case-fold-search on). `names` and `prefixes` are exact; `:` is a",
    "keyword (`:eval`), `nil` and `t` are constants.",
    "`suffixes`: Emacs's risky-local-variable-p (files.el) and the program-naming endings of design 4.4.",
    "`cases`: [name, denied] rows both readers run (the editor refuses the empty name too)."
  ],
